body:
I guess we need `position: -webkit-sticky` to make it work. But doing so introduces another problem on my iPhone XR. 

![RPReplay_Final1561380846 2 2019-06-24 15_19_58](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/499898/60022189-9c690d00-9693-11e9-9dd8-7ef1e518129e.gif)

Look at the bottom. The bottom bars are not aligned to bottom.

```css
position: sticky;
position: -webkit-sticky;
bottom: 0;
```

fixes it(Currently it's `bottom: 4rem`).

From what I understand, `bottom: 0` makes sense, but it doesn't work on desktop Chrome and I don't know why.

